   "stem": {
      "text": "The polar curve \\( r = \\cos{\\left(4 \\theta \\right)} \\) is a rose with 8 petals. Find the exact area of the region enclosed by one petal.",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Multiply",
         [
            "Rational",
            1,
            16
         ],
         "Pi"
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "One petal is traced between consecutive zeros of r, so the angles run from \\( \\theta = - \\frac{\\pi}{8} \\) to \\( \\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{8} \\), where \\( \\cos{\\left(4 \\theta \\right)} = 0 \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99001",
         "rule_named": "limits from zeros of r"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The area is one half the integral of the square of r: \\( A = \\frac{1}{2}\\int_{- \\frac{\\pi}{8}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{8}} \\left(\\cos{\\left(4 \\theta \\right)}\\right)^2\\,d\\theta \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99048",
         "rule_named": "polar area"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Expand the square and use \\( \\sin^2 u = \\tfrac{1}{2}(1 - \\cos 2u) \\) or \\( \\cos^2 u = \\tfrac{1}{2}(1 + \\cos 2u) \\) to integrate, giving \\( A = \\frac{\\pi}{16} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Rational",
               1,
               16
            ],
            "Pi"
         ],
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99004",
         "rule_named": "power reduction"
      }
   ],
